# MEMORY — Rules · Facts · Asks
*Budget (above the fold): ≤ 25 KB. That is the design target for a fresh notebook; a mature one may need more, but growth happens by deliberate consolidation WITH {{USER_NAME}}, never by silent trimming. Read by every mentor agent and at every DOMAIN_SESSION PREPARE — read UP TO the HISTORY fold only: `sed -n '1,/^## ── HISTORY/p' mentors/MEMORY.md`. Read a story below the fold only when its ✓ check fails or you need the reasoning: `grep -n '^\*\*L3 ' mentors/MEMORY.md` → read from that line.*
*Write rule: edit an entry in place by ID (count, supersession, status). A NEW rule/fact/ask = one short entry above the fold + its full story appended at the very end of the file under `## Stories added`. Retire = move the entry below the fold. Never add a dated section above the fold; the only dates up here are in this header. Caps: RULES ≤ 40 · FACTS ≤ 25 · NEVER-REPEAT ≤ 25 · open ASKS ≤ 8 — when a cap is reached, retire or merge before adding.*
*Every mentor report answers every ✓ below (PREFLIGHT: one line "pass: L1, L2…" for passes; one line each for fail+fix). [v:N] = violations since adoption; at v:2 the fix must be STRUCTURAL (protocol/curriculum/format edit), not another reminder. Only the principal closes an ask (see ASKS). FACTS: a plan conflicting with a row is wrong by definition. Origin = "their words <date>" when the row records {{USER_NAME}}'s statement, else "mentor <date>".*
*Fold reorganization: <date of last compaction>. Last compaction: <date of last compaction>. Last review write: <date of last review>.*

> **Why this file exists.** A mentor system that records its mistakes in files the plan-generating agent never reads is not learning — it is keeping a diary. This file puts the system's own corrections, facts, and open asks **into the generation path**, so a correction given in week N provably changes behaviour in week N+1. It is deliberately small above the fold; keeping it small is a hard requirement, not a nicety.
>
> **The four sections and their one-line jobs:**
> - **RULES** — every correction {{USER_NAME}} gives becomes a pre-flight RULE. Read by every mentor before it drafts.
> - **FACTS** — binding facts. A plan that contradicts a fact is wrong by definition.
> - **NEVER-REPEAT** — declined items, permanently off the menu.
> - **ASKS** — an open-ask ledger with mechanical, age-based escalation, so a persistent unmet ask escalates itself instead of quietly persisting.
>
> **The fold.** One fixed line — `## ── HISTORY (on demand; agents do not read past this line) ──` — splits this file. Above it: the short current picture, within budget. Below it: every retired entry and every full story, verbatim, never deleted. Agents stop at the fold and go below it only by ID. The WEEKLY_REVIEW budget check measures the top half and fixes overruns by moving content below the fold, never by deleting it.

