> **Write rule.** Any principal correction (a "this is wrong" flag, a factual error caught, a "weakly planned / mundane" rebuke, a contradicted fact) MUST produce a new rule or increment an existing rule's `[v:N]` count **in the same JOURNAL/review pass**. No correction leaves the session unrecorded.
>
> **Recurrence escalation.** When a rule reaches `[v:2]` after adoption, its phrasing has failed — the fix must become STRUCTURAL (a protocol edit, a curriculum edit, a file-format change), not another prose reminder. Mark it `[v:2 → STRUCTURAL YYYY-MM-DD]`.
>
> **Retirement.** At each SEASON_TRANSITION: retire rules absorbed into protocol/curriculum (move the entry below the fold), merge duplicates, delete wrong ones. Cap ≤ 40 active.

