> **What this is.** The short list of load-bearing facts {{USER_NAME}} has stated that a fresh-drafted plan must never contradict. Forgetting failures (re-proposing done work, re-asserting a corrected fact) happen because facts live only in prose the drafting agent doesn't reread, or get overridden by a fresh draft.
