> **Canonical ownership (P8).** This section is the SINGLE ledger for open recurring asks and their ages. `coordinator_state.md` may reference an ask for cross-domain context but does not re-track its age/owner/status. One ask, one home.
>
> **The escalation rule (mechanical, not judgment).** Age = the number of WEEKLY_REVIEWs the ask has been open; increment by 1 at each review until closed.
> - **Age 0–1:** normal — an owner is assigned, a deliverable named.
> - **Age 2:** ESCALATION. A named mentor owns it with a specific weekly deliverable. Surfaced at Checkpoint 1 as an escalation, not a status line.
> - **Age 3+:** BLOCKING. It becomes a mandatory Mentor Challenge at Checkpoint 2 — the coordinator must present why it keeps failing and propose a structural change (drop it, change owner, change the approach). An ask cannot silently persist past age 3.
>
> **Close rule — only the principal closes an ask.** An ask closes ONLY with a shipped artifact + {{USER_NAME}}'s explicit confirmation. "Owner assigned" is not closed. "Mentor thinks it's handled" is not closed. Self-declared resolution is prohibited; the first time a mentor breaks this, it becomes a RULE above. Closed asks move below the fold with the closing artifact named. Cap ≤ 8 open.

